const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文研究股利价格比与未来股利、折现率和回报预期之间的分解关系。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“The Dividend-Price Ratio and Expectations of Future Dividends and Discount Factors” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/17.1.27",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2004) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2004) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"研究框架围绕估值恒等式展开，把比率的变动与未来现金流和贴现成分的预期联系起来。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “The Dividend-Price Ratio and Expectations of Future Dividends and Discount Factors”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/17.1.27",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2004) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2004) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"核心是股利、价格、再投资与频率口径；这些定义会决定比率是否与原研究中的对象一致。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “The Dividend-Price Ratio and Expectations of Future Dividends and Discount Factors”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/17.1.27",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2004) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2004) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"比率可以携带关于未来成分的联合信息，但来源并不把它说成单变量、无条件的方向性预测器。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “The Dividend-Price Ratio and Expectations of Future Dividends and Discount Factors”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/17.1.27",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2004) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2004) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"统一股利定义、价格日历、对数变换和样本起点，并明确预测回归的持有期是否重叠。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “The Dividend-Price Ratio and Expectations of Future Dividends and Discount Factors”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/17.1.27",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2004) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2004) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Review of Financial Studies (2004)。估值比率会受会计、分配政策和市场制度影响，跨国家或资产类别比较需重新验证。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Review of Financial Studies (2004) for “The Dividend-Price Ratio and Expectations of Future Dividends and Discount Factors”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/17.1.27",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2004) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2004) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“The Dividend-Price Ratio and Expectations of Future Dividends and Discount Factors”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。估值比率会受会计、分配政策和市场制度影响，跨国家或资产类别比较需重新验证。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “The Dividend-Price Ratio and Expectations of Future Dividends and Discount Factors”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
